# yours.list — your files, the ones `vikix snapshot` keeps a history of.
#
# Paths are relative to your home folder. A folder means everything in
# it, apart from what the exclude list in bin/vikix leaves out (Vikix's
# own links in ~/.stumpwm.d, logs, backups). With this history, any
# change to these files, by you or by an AI agent, can be seen with
# `vikix changes` and taken back with `vikix undo`.

.stumpwm.d                  # user.lisp, and any Lisp files of your own
.config/alacritty
.config/picom
.config/dunst
.config/rofi
.config/vikix/keyboard
.config/vikix/wallpaper      # the wallpaper you chose (a link to it)
.config/gammastep            # night light times and colours
.config/mimeapps.list
.config/vikix/backup          # where backups go (not the password: that stays out of here)
.config/vikix/backup-exclude  # what they leave out
.config/vikix/features        # the features you chose (vikix add, vikix remove)
.config/vikix/packages-skip   # packages you dropped (vikix pkg drop), kept out
.config/vikix/optional        # before 0.46: the optional ones (now in features)
.config/vikix/windows         # where the Windows VM's disk is
.config/vikix/webapps         # your web apps (vikix webapp)
.config/vikix/ai              # which model AI on keys uses (Super+i)
.config/vikix/agent           # which AI agent Super+a starts (vikix agent --default)
.config/vikix/dictation       # dictation's model (vikix dictate models)
.config/vikix/voice           # the voice, and when a new chat starts (vikix voice)
.config/vikix/notes           # the folder note reads, and what it skips (note index)
.config/nvim                  # Neovim: your plugins and settings, and the plugins' versions (not when it's a git clone: that has its own history)
# The agents' own settings, file by file (their folders also hold logins):
# an agent could change its own permissions or hooks, and this shows it.
.claude/settings.json
.claude/CLAUDE.md
.codex/config.toml
.gemini/settings.json
.gemini/GEMINI.md
.config/opencode/opencode.json
.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc
.aider.conf.yml
.Xresources
.bashrc
.bash_profile
